  "worked_solution": "To find the complex conjugate of a vector, we take the complex conjugate of the entries of the vector. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\overset{\u2015}{x}}_{1} & =\\overset{\u2015}{[\\begin{aligned}4+3\\text{i} \\\\ -1+3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\u2015}{4+3\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{\u2015}{-1+3\\text{i}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4-3\\text{i} \\\\ -1-3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the second vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{i}\\cdot {x}_{2} & =\\text{i}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5+4\\text{i} \\\\ -4-3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5\\text{i}+4{\\text{i}}^{2} \\\\ -4\\text{i}-3{\\text{i}}^{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4+5\\text{i} \\\\ 3-4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\overset{\u2015}{x}}_{1}+\\text{i}\\cdot {x}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}4-3\\text{i} \\\\ -1-3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-4+5\\text{i} \\\\ 3-4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\text{i} \\\\ 2-7\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
